Compact labels written with a wrong-case prefix (`:labelRetry`,
`:LabelRetry`) are not recognized as labels at run time:
label_keyword_form (error) over the whole token. The correct compact
`:LABELRetry` (only the prefix is case-checked) and a plain
`sLabelText` identifier do not flag (diag.label_keyword_form). Records
how the Branch literals against these labels are judged.
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ReadLoop;
	:DECLARE nRound, sLabelText;
	nRound := 0;
	sLabelText := "caption";
	:labelRetry;
	:LabelAgain;
	:LABELRetry;
	nRound := nRound + 1;
	:IF nRound < 3;
		Branch("LABELRetry");
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nRound;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ReadLoop;
	:DECLARE nRound, sLabelText;

	nRound := 0;
	sLabelText := "caption";
	:labelRetry;
	:LabelAgain;
	:LABELRetry;
	nRound := nRound + 1;

	:IF nRound < 3;
		Branch("LABELRetry");
	:ENDIF;

	:RETURN nRound;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
